    "design_notes": "Kept the screenshots' bezel-in-bezel dark green CRT look, status header, left status rail, sector scope with range rings, right-hand status stack and the F1–F12 key strip, but recompressed everything to a single 100vh viewport: type and padding are tighter, the three left rail panels are merged into one grouped-readout panel, the fire-status and ID keys are moved to the flanks, and the brass warning plate now shares the function-key row so no vertical space is wasted. Scrolling now happens inside the slots (each keeps a min-height and its own overflow) rather than on the page; below 1040px wide or 600px tall the layout falls back to a stacked, scrollable form. From the profile: the eight track columns in order (TRK, SPD, ALT, TYPE, ID, FIRE STATUS, TTI, PK), the four identification states with their tones (own forces/friendly blue-green, unknown amber, enemy red), the fixed 120° tilt-only sector with 150/100/50 km class detection and 70/50/20 km engagement rings, and a decision strip sized for the seven-step commit sequence plus tilt; no correlate/auto-ID affordances are provided since those are automatic. All Hebrew captions, vendor wording, trajectory-analysis content and the diagnostics tree from the screenshots were dropped or generalised.",
